sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-model-fidelity> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Hamant et al. (2008), Bozorg et al. (2014), Sampathkumar et al. (2014), Uyttewaal et al. (2012), Heisler et al. (2010) & Louveaux et al. (2016) shoot apical meristem shell stress tensor, stress-vs-strain CMT alignment, katanin boundary morphogenesis and PIN1/CMT co-alignment on a growing L1 cellular vertex mesh — Model fidelity to source: 70/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credited: the vertex mesh implements recognisable published mechanisms — Hookean anticlinal wall tension with Lockhart creep above a yield strain (`wall_state` L674-682, `step_fields` L819-835), the Batchelor virial wall-stress tensor sum_e T_e l_e t⊗t and its principal axis as the CMT cue (`cell_tensors` L722-747), nematic S = gamma a / (gamma a + 2 D_theta) in the Bozorg Eq. 12 form (L790-798), cellulose reinforcement of CMT-parallel walls closing the stress feedback loop (`_wall_stiffness` L665-672), Heisler's stress-based PIN1 rule as a softmax on wall tension with PIN1-polar auxin fluxes (`pin1_state` L749-770, transport L803-817), division along sigma_1 with an Errera fallback (L1062-1093) and a correct, unit-tested T1 flip (`apply_t1` L922-965); Laws 4-5 are machine-checked. Deductions: the mesh is 2D, so the saddle's negative Gaussian curvature is replaced by an anisotropic boundary pre-strain (L1046-1047) — the K < 0 vs K > 0 physics of Law 1 is not on the mesh (-8); the v2 'FEM' field is a sum of hand-placed Gaussians (L325-330) and the per-zone principal stresses are prescribed constants (L173-215), not solved from turgor and curvature (-8); the 5-condition sweep is a closed-form fit with uncited exponents 1.45 / 0.68 / 15.95 and literal strain-cue and oryzalin values (L412-432) (-6); the Bozorg stress-vs-strain discrimination does not emerge on the mesh (ablation CMT circumferential 0.985 vs 0.968 for the strain cue; L1137-1155 report it) (-4); auxin feedback on growth is phenomenological (k_aux on creep) and no auxin maximum forms (-2); in-plane turgor is a small residual (P = 0.15) with periclinal area elasticity standing in for the out-of-plane pressure load (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py L173–L215: Per-zone sigma_1 / sigma_2 are prescribed multiples of sigma_0 (e.g. 1.90, 0.30) rather than solved from curvature and turgor <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L173-L215>",
            "2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py L325–L330: '2D FEM' anisotropy field is three hand-placed Gaussian weights plus a lateral_compression constant — not a finite-element solve <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L325-L330>",
            "2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py L412–L432: 5-condition sweep: closed-form S_pred / depth with uncited constants; strain-cue and oryzalin S, depth, cos^2 and r are literals <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L412-L432>" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-model-fidelity-3> ;
        pk:hasScore "0.7"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-model-fidelity-1> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py L509–L985" ;
        dct:description "L1VertexTissue: Voronoi-jittered hex patch, Hookean walls with rest lengths, virial stress tensor, CMT/S dynamics, PIN1 softmax, auxin transport, Lockhart creep, division, T1 flip" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L509-L985> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-model-fidelity-2> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py L1020–L1156" ;
        dct:description "simulate_l1_vertex_patch: zone stress -> boundary pre-strain -> walls -> M_c -> CMT -> reinforcement -> PIN1 -> auxin -> growth -> division chain; 2D only, curvature not represented (L1046-1047)" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py#L1020-L1156> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-model-fidelity-3> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_036_microtubule_stress_meristem.lean L165–L268" ;
        dct:description "Laws 4-5 (PIN1/CMT co-alignment under anisotropic wall tension incl. gamma_MT = 0; division/T1 Euler invariant), lean-verified, 0 sorrys" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_036_microtubule_stress_meristem.lean#L165-L268> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 036 Pass 3 builder + primary assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

